Smart Study Planner is a simple Java program you run from your computer's command line. 
It helps students figure out what subjects to focus on each day. The program assigns a priority score to each subject. 
It calculates this score based on how hard the subject is, how many days are left before the exam, and how many credits it's worth.
Then, it divides up the study hours you have available among the subjects, giving more time to the ones with higher priority.
